<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🍂 LIVE LEAF COLOR</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE LEAF COLOR</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/leaf_color/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Satellite-derived seasonal vegetation state. The continuous color scale represents the changing seasonal condition of vegetated land, from winter dormancy through spring emergence, active growth, autumn coloration, leaf drop, and return to dormancy. Color represents a satellite-derived phenological state and should not be interpreted as the exact color of every individual tree. Every basin land pixel is painted: cloudy or missing pixels take a smooth blend of today's surrounding observed land. Only Great-Lakes water stays transparent.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NASA MODIS Aqua MYD13A1/MYD09A1 via Planetary Computer (global, 500 m)).<br/><b>Data time:</b> VI composite start 2026-08-05 (+16d window); reflectance 2026-08-13 (+8d); retrieved 2026-09-25 03:55 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> leaf-v6-1ce56c63a4cc<br/><b>Status:</b> LATEST AVAILABLE COMPOSITE</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🍂 LIVE LEAF COLOR — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Leaf_Color.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>21600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
